        "main_video_caption_en": "The island of Gorée lies off the coast of Senegal, opposite Dakar. From the 15th to the 19th century, it was the largest slave-trading centre on the African coast. Ruled in succession by the Portuguese, Dutch, English and French, its architecture is characterized by the contrast between the grim slave-quarters and the elegant houses of the slave traders. Today it continues to serve as a reminder of human exploitation and as a  ...\n\nSource: UNESCO TV / © NHK Nippon Hoso Kyokai\nURL: https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/26/",
        "videos_urls": [
            "https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/WKdnvw1uymg"
        ],
